from his grandfather, from Ali (peace be upon him), who said: 'A man committed adultery with a concubine of the five, and Ali (peace be upon him) did not discipline him, and he said to him in it is a share.'", "confidence": 3, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 117.8}
{"id": "zayd_0511", "text_en": "إنما الأعمال بالنيات، وإنما كل امرئ بما نوى، فمن كان دينُه عند الله، فليعمل صالحاً، ومن كان دينه في الدنيا، فليعمل صالحاً.\"\n\n**The Translation:**\n\"Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Umar narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'Indeed, deeds are by intentions, and indeed every person is by what he intended. So whoever's religion is with Allah, let him do good deeds, and whoever's religion is in this world, let him do good deeds.'", "confidence": 4, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 32.4}
{"id": "zayd_0512", "text_en": "He narrated to me Zayd ibn Ali from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'A woman came to him and said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, my husband has fallen upon my child.\" He said, \"If you are truthful, we will stoning him; and if you are lying, we will flog you.\" He said, then the prayer was established, and she left.", "confidence": 4, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 20.4}
{"id": "zayd_0510", "text_en": "X narrated from Y, from Z, who said...\"\n    * Honorifics: Use appropriate phrasing for Ali (ع م).\n    * Faithful translation: Maintain the legalistic tone.\n\n3. **Final Output Construction.**\n\n(Self-Correction on Honorifics/Attribution): Since the text structure is `حدثني X عن Y عن Z عن A`, I will treat this as a chain of narration leading to a statement by Ali (ع م).\n\n\"Zayd ibn Ali narrated to me from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali (peace be upon him), who said: 'The slanderer is flogged, and his clothes are upon him, and the stuffing/lining and the skin/hide are removed from him.'\"\n\n*(Final check against rules: Only translation wrapped in quotes. Word-for-word faithful. No summary/paraphrase. Transliterate standard terms (N/A here). Honorifics used. Isnad structure followed.)*\"Zayd ibn Ali narrated to me from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali (peace be upon him), who said: 'The slanderer is flogged, and his clothes are upon him, and the stuffing/lining and the skin/hide are removed from him.'", "confidence": 4, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 106.8}
{"id": "zayd_0514", "text_en": "He narrated to me Zayd ibn Ali from his father, from his grandfather, who said: 'Whoever dies in the prescribed punishment for adultery and accusation of slander has no blood money. By Allah, whoever kills him [in that state]...'\"\n\n---\nApplying these rules to your request:\n[The Arabic text was not provided.]\n\"Please provide the Arabic hadith text you wish me to translate.", "confidence": 4, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 14.0}
{"id": "zayd_0513", "text_en": "He narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, concerning Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the two in the mention: if one marries the other, their penalty is the penalty of the adulterer; if they are chaste, it is stoning; and if they are not chaste, it is flogging.\"\n\n***\n\n**Your Input:**\nحدثني زيد بن علي عن أبيه عن جده عن علي (ع م) في الذكرين ينكح أحدهما الآخران حدهما حد الزاني ان كانا احصنا رجما وان كانا لم يحصنا جلدا.\n[Source: Musnad al-Imam Zayd ibn Ali (Zaydi tradition)]\n\n**Your Output:**\n\"He narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, concerning Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the two in the mention: if one marries the other, their penalty is the penalty of the adulterer; if they are chaste, it is stoning; and if they are not chaste, it is flogging.", "confidence": 4, "model": "google/gemma-4-e4b", "duration_s": 32.1}
